{"id":"chatcmpl-e905c9a5-449d-4381-b488-2eef8d83e69f","object":"chat.completion","created":1795245112,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a cross-validation strategy for medical image interpretation: querying multiple independent expert models on the same diagnostic question and requiring convergent evidence before committing to an answer. The key insight is that laterality/direction questions benefit from explicit directional framing in prompts and independent confirmation to reduce single-model bias. The pattern generalizes to any visual QA task where a binary or directional finding must be determined from an image.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a question asks for a directional or laterality finding, explicitly frame the query in terms of the two candidate directions to force a discriminative judgment rather than a vague description.\",\n    \"Query at least two independent expert models on the same diagnostic question and only answer when their conclusions converge, treating disagreement as a signal to re-examine.\",\n    \"Match the imaging view referenced in the prompt to the tool's expected input (e.g., lateral vs. AP) and note when the view may limit assessability of the finding.\",\n    \"Use the released benchmark feedback as a post-hoc consistency check against the converged model answer to confirm the reasoning path was sound.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA\": \"Frame directional/laterality questions explicitly; cross-validate with two independent expert models; prefer convergent evidence over single-model confidence.\",\n    \"Binary visual classification\": \"Convert open-ended description requests into forced-choice directional prompts to reduce ambiguity and improve discriminative accuracy.\",\n    \"Multi-model consensus tasks\": \"Treat independent model agreement as a reliability signal; when models disagree, flag for re-examination rather than defaulting to one.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the question's directional framing (right vs. left, convexity direction) is explicitly stated in every tool query.\",\n    \"Verify that at least two independent sources agree on the finding before finalizing the answer.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":487,"total_tokens":873,"completion_tokens":386,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":487},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":386}}}